{
  "about": "The fonts every Windows 10 and 11 comes with, by family name (the names a page asks for them by, the older ones a weight or width once had its own name under among them). Every profile in Noor shows these (see main/fonts.js); the fonts Windows adds with a language are in rules/font-pool.json, with the other programs' a profile may have. A family followed by style words only ('Segoe UI Semibold', 'Bahnschrift Light Condensed') counts as the family; a name that starts with one of the prefixes (families only Microsoft makes, whose older names Windows cuts to 31 letters: 'Segoe UI Variable Display Semib') counts too.",
